# Mod outpost — Praxis runs a briefing-room rather than a rally.
# Sharper, colder, fewer hand-gestures. Audience members enrolled
# into Mods receive a clipboard on entry.

== mod_outpost
  cast: Praxis
  setting: ModOutpost

<broadcast: cohort(Mods)>
  NARRATOR
    The fans roar. Every monitor on the back wall is tiled with the
    same image — the Plaza, in real time, including you.

PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 120s, advance on: quorum(6) [speech(go), gesture(Cue)])
  (Run a briefing. Assign each Mod a watch-target — name an actual
   Chatter audience-member they're now responsible for monitoring.
   The Playwright watches for resistance and marks reluctant Mods
   as defection candidates.)

# Praxis publishes the rules of engagement. Only mods can hear.
<broadcast: cohort(Mods) and location(ModOutpost)>
  NARRATOR
    A monitor labeled CALIBRATION blinks. Nobody else has noticed.

# Chatters hear, distantly, what Praxis is saying about them.
<broadcast: cohort(Chatters)>
  PRAXIS
    (over the relay)
    There is no conspiracy. There are people screaming because order
    inconveniences them. Stand down. Go home. Eat something.

* Praxis names a specific chatter and dispatches a watch team.
  -> mod_dispatch
* Praxis admits her people have been coming back wrong.
  -> mod_confession

== mod_dispatch
  cast: Praxis
  setting: ModOutpost

PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 90s, advance on: any [gesture(stand), speech(vex)])
  (Dispatch three Mods toward the Chatter Camp. Tell them: "Watch.
   Don't engage. The first Mod who engages tonight gets pulled.")

<set: Praxis.trusts.Mods += 10>

# The dispatched mods cross broadcast scope to the chatters.
<broadcast: cohort(Chatters)>
  NARRATOR
    Three figures in matching jackets cross the Plaza in step.
    Nobody on the chatter side is reassured by this.

* The watch team turns back when one of them sees the door.
  -> mod_at_door
* The watch team engages anyway — Praxis loses control.
  -> faction_war
* The Playwright pulls four Mods aside.
  -> defection

== mod_confession
  cast: Praxis
  setting: ModOutpost

PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 90s, advance on: quorum(4) [speech(go), gesture(nod)])
  (Crack. Tell the Mods that three of theirs came back from a
   chatter raid last month "different." Pick a real Mod
   audience-member and address them as one of the affected. Then
   apologize — actually apologize — for using them as cover.)

<set: Praxis.knows.motherboard_named = true>
<set: Praxis.trusts.Mods -= 15>

<broadcast: cohort(Mods) and location(ModOutpost)>
  PRAXIS
    The thing on the monitor labeled CALIBRATION isn't a calibration
    tool. I don't know what it is. I have been pretending I did.

* Praxis leads four Mods toward the Plaza door.
  -> mod_at_door
* Praxis stands down — Mods may break ranks toward Defection.
  -> defection

== mod_at_door
  cast: Praxis
  setting: Plaza

<broadcast: location(Plaza)>
  NARRATOR
    Mod boots in the Plaza. The door behind the fountain hangs open.

PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 60s, advance on: any [speech(motherboard), gesture(recoil)])
  (Approach. Bring the four. Look in. The Playwright cues a cyborg
   into the doorway again.)

CYBORG
  (improv duration: 30s, advance on: quorum(3) [gesture(recoil)])
  (Stand. Turn. Address Praxis by her first name — which she has
   not, tonight, given.)

<set: Praxis.knows.motherboard_named = true>

-> defection

== praxis_committed
  cast: Praxis
  setting: ModOutpost

PRAXIS
  (low, to the front row of Mods)
  Whatever I order you to do for the rest of the night — if I look
  through you when I'm saying it, refuse. That's the protocol now.
